      "title": "Part- Time Lecturer (College of Arts and Sciences)",
      "description": "Part- Time Lecturer (College of Arts and Sciences) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Part- Time Lecturer (College of Arts and Sciences) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Aug 31 2026 Closing on: Sep 17 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Part-Time Lecturer (College of Arts and Sciences) Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Mathematics and Statistics Department: College of Arts and Sciences Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Department of Mathematics & Statistics is seeking a part-time lecturer to teach specific Math & Stat courses. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Teach contractual load of courses as assigned by the department or school. Assign and submit grades in accordance with established University schedules. Keep posted office hours during the week which are scheduled at times most beneficial to students. Provide enrollment data and such other information as corrected class lists, etc. as may be required by the University. Engage in pursuits that enable them to remain current in their respective disciplines. Confer periodically with the Department Head/School Director on curriculum and instruction issues. Provide other support service to the department, school and/oruniversity, if applicable. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Mathematics or related disciplines. Preferred Qualifications: N/A Special Instructions: Applicants should submit a cover letter and resume. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert e21a825f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdow