      "title": "Want to hear about jobs like this one?",
      "description": "College Data Analyst, Accreditation & Learning Assessment - CHHS - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode College Data Analyst, Accreditation & Learning Assessment - CHHS Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Health and Human Serv Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Aug 26 2026 Closing on: Sep 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: College Data Analyst, Accreditation & Learning Assessment - CHHS Employee Classification: PT Pay Grade: PT 08 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Health and Human Service Department: College of Health and Human Serv Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Coordinate and implement the development and maintenance of databases, including analyzing and reporting data needed to support accreditation procedures and processes as well as student learning assessment, planning, and improvement activities within the assigned college. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Support accreditation procedures and processes for the assigned college, including compiling, collecting, and analyzing information and data for statistical reports. Develop and maintain databases of accreditation-related information. Support faculty and staff in their work to identify, store, and analyze student learning assessment data. Support faculty and staff in database use, data analysis, and data maintenance. Manipulate and create statistical reports from SCT Banner, EMU, and other appropriate information systems for accreditation purposes. Identify, gather, and organize data to provide accurate and timely information. Serve as the key contact for staff and faculty for data reporting. Meet with faculty, staff, and appropriate accrediting body representatives, as needed, regarding assessment and accreditation issues. Conduct or participate in workshops, committees, and conferences designed for the area of assignment. Serve as liaison to other departments and colleges within EMU for accreditation purposes. Perform technical data support duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of statistical analysis, quantitative and analytical processes, data collection/management, and excellent organizational communication skills acquired through the completion of a bachelor's degree in business administration, technology, engineering, education or a related field, is necessary. A minimum of 3 years of experience with database development and maintenance is required. Ability to communicate both orally and in writing (including electronically) at a high level of competency is required. Ability to handle multiple tasks efficiently with attention to detail and to meet deadlines is essential. Knowledge and success in implementation of models, processes and techniques used to develop a continuous improvement environment is necessary. Ability to work in a team environment is necessary. Preferred Qualifications: A master's degree in these or a related field, is preferred. Knowledge of EMU data and electronic systems and programs in the assigned college is preferred. Experience with an accreditation process is preferred. Special Instructions: N/A Appointment Percentage: 92% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 1fe0521b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Health and Human Serv College of Health and Human Serv Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) cba52a16 Last Name (required) 2a3bfa22 Email (required) 07d1691a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the In