    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/graduate-assistant-fashion-marketing-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant (Fashion Marketing)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant (Fashion Marketing) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Graduate Assistant (Fashion Marketing) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Research Admin and Grad School Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Opening on: Jul 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Graduate Assistant (Fashion Marketing) Employee Classification: GS - Graduate Student - Stipend Pay Grade: GS 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Graduate School Department: Research Admin and Grad School Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The School of Technology & Professional Services Management invites applications for a Graduate Assistant (GA) to support the Fashion Marketing Innovation Program. This position provides instructional, laboratory, and program support while offering valuable professional experience in higher education and the fashion industry. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty and students in apparel construction, textiles, product development, and fashion merchandising. The position is 50% for Fall 2026. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Assist faculty with undergraduate courses in fashion design, sewing and construction, textiles, product development, and merchandising. - Provide instruction and guidance to students during laboratory sessions, including garment construction techniques and the proper use of sewing equipment. - Support product development activities including specification sheets, quality evaluation, garment analysis, and apparel production processes. - Assist with textile identification, fabric performance testing, and materials evaluation. - Support merchandising projects including visual merchandising, trend forecasting, retail analysis, and consumer research. - Prepare laboratories for instruction and maintain sewing machines, equipment, supplies, and inventory. - Support student recruitment events, open houses, portfolio shows, and outreach activities. - Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: - Admission to or enrollment in an EMU graduate program. - Bachelor's degree in Fashion Merchandising, Fashion Design, Apparel Product Development, Textiles, or related field. - Knowledge of sewing, apparel construction, textiles, product development, and merchandising. - Excellent communication and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience in fashion retail, apparel manufacturing, product development, or textile testing. - Experience with sewing equipment and fashion technology terminology. - Prior teaching, tutoring, or laboratory assistant experience is a plus. Appointment 10 hours per week during the academic semester. Compensation in accordance with EMU Graduate Assistant policies. Application Materials Letter of interest, resumé/CV, three references, and graduate enrollment information. Special Instructions: Submit Transcript and email of interest Appointment Percentage: 50% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 5486f78b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Research Admin and Grad School Research Admin and Grad School Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 05738911 Last Name (required) b50e7a2e Email (required) caa243fa Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development function serving business students, with direct responsibility for internship placement, professional development programming, and the cultivation of strong, lasting relationships between the College and the employer community. This role is the primary architect of the business student experience that connects classroom learning to professional practice - from securing and overseeing internships, to running signature events such as Company Days, etiquette lunch and dinners, the executive speaker series, and facilitating executive mentoring and preparing students to compete confidently for the roles they want after graduation. Health & Safety Specialist Public Safety Develop, revise, implement and monitor University health, safety and environmental programs/activities to ensure compliance with federal, state and local occupational safety, health and environmental regulations. Administrative Secretary College of Education Provide secretarial services and administrative assistance to Dean, Executive Director, or equivalent-level administrator. Athletic Academic Program Specialist Intercollegiate Athletics Assist in the administ