    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/building-automation-specialist-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Building Automation Specialist",
      "description": "Building Automation Specialist - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Home Working at EMU Benefits & Wellness About HR Existing Applicant Log-in Kiosk mode Building Automation Specialist Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 7 2025 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Building Automation Specialist Employee Classification: FM Pay Grade: FM 24 Division: Business and Finance Subdivision: General Maint and Repr Department: Facilities Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Position is responsible for the monitoring, adjustment, programming, repair, and maintenance of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration (HVAC/R) automation and building integration systems. Position requires a variety of skilled and technical work related to the maintenance, repair, programming, and installation of HVAC/R automation and building integration systems and associated components. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Install, repair, and maintain DDC equipment related to HVAC/R and building integration systems. Use a workstation or portable terminal to command points, evaluate programs, backup databases, and update changes or additions to the databases. Use automated building management software to monitor, troubleshoot, correct, modify, and improve HVAC/R and building integration systems operations. Interpret, modify, and write software to control HVAC/R and building integration systems and equipment. Evaluate sequences of operation and assess the probability of the sequences functioning properly with DDC, pneumatic, and electric control systems when applied to HVAC/R equipment. Create, modify, and update computer graphic displays as needed to accommodate system additions and modifications. Read and interpret blueprints, schematics, diagrams, drawings, manufacturers' specifications, and written and verbal instructions related to HVAC/R and building integration systems. Assist the Principle Plant Engineer-Energy Conservation and Sustainability with reviewing, developing, evaluating, and implementing energy conservation and sustainability initiatives. Diagnose HVAC and building integration system problems, including verifying operations of dampers, valves, actuators, coils, fans, pumps, heat exchangers, VAV boxes, airflow devices, water flow devices, thermostats, and other HVAC/R components. Prepare reports and maintain records and logs as may be required. Plan and coordinate work and procure materials and equipment required to install new systems and repair and maintain existing systems. Reclaim and recharge refrigerant systems as needed. Use basic hand and power tools. Operate motor vehicles. Perform periodic visual inspections and maintain cleanliness of work and storage areas, mechanical rooms and all tools, vehicles and equipment used in the performance of duties. Report any damage, malfunction, irregularities, or potential hazards in buildings, grounds, equipment, vehicles, or supplies to supervisor. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Proficiency in reading, writing, and mathematical processes typically acquired through the completion of a high school education and associated technical training is necessary. An Associate Degree in HVAC or documented, advanced factory training in DDC and/or building integration systems is required. Three (3) years within the last Five (5) years of verifiable, directly related work experience performing the installation, inspection, testing, programming, maintenance, and repair of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration automation and building integration systems is necessary. Three (3) years within the last five (5) years of verifiable experience with Trane Tracer Summit, Johnson Metasys, Honeywell Excel 5000/EBI, BACnet, LonWorks, and/or other building automation systems including configuration and programming is required. Experience in programming building automation and building integration systems including web based, proprietary, and library based languages. Personal computer skills utilizing word processing and spreadsheet applications, CAD applications, and file management functions are necessary. Possession of a valid Michigan Driver's license is necessary. Ability to meet departmental standards of reasonable personal hygiene is necessary. The ability to perform physically active work of a medium nature, requiring frequent walking, climbing, pushing, pulling, stooping, kneeling and crouching activity to performing routine work functions and lifting requiring up to 50 pounds frequently and occasionally 100 pounds of force to move and/or transport equipment and supplies is necessary. EPA Section 608, Universal Refrigerant Certification is required. Preferred Qualifications: R410a Certification is desirable. Additional Information: Salary: FM 24 = $47.12 an hour/$98,010.00 annually. Shift: Monday - Friday, 7:30 AM to 4:00 PM Location: Physical Plant Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 0f779cec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Categories Business & Finance Business & Finance First Name (required) 485c0d1e Last Name (required) 2b86c37a Email (required) 12879cdf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. COB Director of Internships, Career Services & Professional Development College of Business The Director of Internships, Career Services and Professional Development leads the College of Business' career and professional development function serving business students, with direct responsibility for internship placement, professional development programming, and the cultivation of strong, lasting relationships between the College and the employer community. This role is the primary architect of the business student experience that connects classroom learning to professional practice - from securing and overseeing internships, to running signature events such as Company Days, etiquette lunch and dinners, the executive speaker series, and facilitating executive mentoring and preparing students to compete confidently for the roles they want after graduation. Health & Safety Specialist Public Safety Develop, revise, implement and monitor University health, safety and environmental programs/activities to ensure compliance with federal, state and local occupational safety, health and environmental regulations. Administrative Secretary College of Education Provide secretarial services and administrative assistance to Dean, Executive Director, or equivalent-level administrator. Athletic Academic Program Specialist Intercollegiate Athletics Assist in the administration as well as the continuous development and implementation of a comprehensive support program for all student-athletes in compliance with University, MAC and NCAA regulations. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 14a75c73 Last Name (required) 2792de87 Email (required) 6164236b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Report a Title IX Incident Accessibility Privacy Statement Annual Security Report Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Michigan University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
